(7318730, 1141611, 137576, '<td valign="top">lovely light and and great framing, the figures add so much, the obvious man then the one who appears with a more detailed look. i like the grafiti alien man as well.</td>', 'lovely light and and great framing, the figures add so much, the obvious man then the one who appears with a more detailed look. i like the grafiti alien man as well.', '2015-02-19 18:40:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(7318744, 1141119, 103142, '<td valign="top">Ok -- this is pretty cool. I''m curious what it would look like with more muted colors. I''m guessing it''s better this way. It just makes me curious playing with it with different tones and maybe even b&amp;w. This works for me.</td>', 'Ok -- this is pretty cool. I''m curious what it would look like with more muted colors. I''m guessing it''s better this way. It just makes me curious playing with it with different tones and maybe even b&w. This works for me.', '2015-02-19 19:59:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(7318745, 1141771, 103142, '<td valign="top">I''m guessing that some of the art fiends will see this as nature documentary vs art. Being a nature fan, I have a tendency to find most nature shots more documentary than art, because there are just so many that there''s a been there done that feel.<br/> <br/>This, however, really works for me. The lighting is spectacular. The crop is awesome. And it just makes you feel like you''re flying, as well. Art should evoke something in you. It should make you curious, intrigued, sad, angry, it needs to transcend just simply documenting the world. I''m not sure why this fits in that category for me. But it does. Well done.</td>', 'I''m guessing that some of the art fiends will see this as nature documentary vs art. Being a nature fan, I have a tendency to find most nature shots more documentary than art, because there are just so many that there''s a been there done that feel. This, however, really works for me. The lighting is spectacular. The crop is awesome. And it just makes you feel like you''re flying, as well. Art should evoke something in you. It should make you curious, intrigued, sad, angry, it needs to transcend just simply documenting the world. I''m not sure why this fits in that category for me. But it does. Well done.', '2015-02-19 20:02:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(7318746, 1141264, 103142, '<td valign="top">I''ve been quoting the same types of things in my comments: Art should make you feel something. It should go beyond just documenting the world. This one works for me. Mostly because it just makes me curious. I''m wondering about the story. It could simply just be models modeling dresses, but I''m seeing a much better storyline and I keep looking farther and farther into this trying to find more clues. Well done.</td>', 'I''ve been quoting the same types of things in my comments: Art should make you feel something. It should go beyond just documenting the world. This one works for me. Mostly because it just makes me curious. I''m wondering about the story. It could simply just be models modeling dresses, but I''m seeing a much better storyline and I keep looking farther and farther into this trying to find more clues. Well done.', '2015-02-19 20:04:56.000000', NULL, 1),
