(7320445, 1141879, 24454, '<td valign="top">Oh yes!  I LOVE this one.  It has that soft, ethereal quality that always grabs me, yet it also has a desolate edginess to it that makes it so interesting!  Congratulations on the well-deserved juried honorable mention!<br/> <br/></td>', 'Oh yes!  I LOVE this one.  It has that soft, ethereal quality that always grabs me, yet it also has a desolate edginess to it that makes it so interesting!  Congratulations on the well-deserved juried honorable mention! ', '2015-02-23 12:38:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(7320447, 1141102, 24454, '<td valign="top">Yes!  A wonderful choice for a juried honorable mention!  The ability to create something extraordinary from the ordinary with the use of light, shadows, and mood is a gift indeed!  <br/> <br/></td>', 'Yes!  A wonderful choice for a juried honorable mention!  The ability to create something extraordinary from the ordinary with the use of light, shadows, and mood is a gift indeed!   ', '2015-02-23 12:41:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(7320485, 1141513, 12611, '<td valign="top">I like it. the pen and ink feel- the horse head and tail are terrific. I am guessing that people did not care for the border, the tilt, the title(can''t make sense of the hat equation)- and perhaps the blown out body-into sky feel-something like that. But still quite a worthy shot.</td>', 'I like it. the pen and ink feel- the horse head and tail are terrific. I am guessing that people did not care for the border, the tilt, the title(can''t make sense of the hat equation)- and perhaps the blown out body-into sky feel-something like that. But still quite a worthy shot.', '2015-02-23 14:13:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(7320487, 1141106, 12611, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by bvy:</b></div><hr/><i> Sorely underappreciated. Proud and sad to be your only ten. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>exactly-(even though your response was well taken). such great details- the older woman dancing, the topless bird flipper, the stoned eyes-all very good.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2015-02-23 14:17:39.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by bvy: Sorely underappreciated. Proud and sad to be your only ten.  exactly-(even though your response was well taken). such great details- the older woman dancing, the topless bird flipper, the stoned eyes-all very good.', '2015-02-23 14:16:39.000000', '2015-02-23 14:17:39.000000', 0),
(7320497, 1141095, 50695, '<td valign="top">Somehow, I cropped my own remarks on the jury thread. What I said was that this photo is inside out. The elements on the edges would normally lead into the center, but instead they lead out of frame. This gives us a new idea of what the "center" is.</td>', 'Somehow, I cropped my own remarks on the jury thread. What I said was that this photo is inside out. The elements on the edges would normally lead into the center, but instead they lead out of frame. This gives us a new idea of what the "center" is.', '2015-02-23 14:45:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(7320506, 1141941, 124815, '<td valign="top">What a great marriage between the image and its title! <br/> <br/>Ive seen another version of this shot and I liked it then and I like this one even more. A good photograph stays with you. <br/>What comes to my mind immediately is the feel of a Melville movie or a French gangster movies  The "Sicilian Clan" is one of them with its music by Ennio Morricone. As we watch from the balcony edge the suspects going to their fateful destination I hear the repetitive theme song spasmodically following every step, every thought, every breath and a great fog covers our eyes or the François de Roubaix theme song of Melvilles "Le Samourai" with its profound feeling of solitude. <br/> <br/>The fact that this photograph worked on my mind so quickly making all these connections is the greatest accolade that I can give you.</td>', 'What a great marriage between the image and its title!  Ive seen another version of this shot and I liked it then and I like this one even more. A good photograph stays with you. What comes to my mind immediately is the feel of a Melville movie or a French gangster movies  The "Sicilian Clan" is one of them with its music by Ennio Morricone. As we watch from the balcony edge the suspects going to their fateful destination I hear the repetitive theme song spasmodically following every step, every thought, every breath and a great fog covers our eyes or the François de Roubaix theme song of Melvilles "Le Samourai" with its profound feeling of solitude.  The fact that this photograph worked on my mind so quickly making all these connections is the greatest accolade that I can give you.', '2015-02-23 15:07:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(7320507, 1141960, 124815, '<td valign="top">I have to ignore the title that does not help me and just look at this still. A behind the scene moment, the film director at work. The picture is ultra saturated and has an unappealing fuzziness that makes sense though in the context I just mentioned. An interesting find.</td>', 'I have to ignore the title that does not help me and just look at this still. A behind the scene moment, the film director at work. The picture is ultra saturated and has an unappealing fuzziness that makes sense though in the context I just mentioned. An interesting find.', '2015-02-23 15:07:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(7320508, 1141095, 124815, '<td valign="top">Our eyes perceive this image in a pinwheel movement trying to find a resting place to give us an answer but there is not such thing and we are forever searching. There are all kinds of elements here. There is graciousness, power, tiredness, acceptance, fear, violence and in the end some hope. Its an imperfect photograph of an imperfect world. It belongs to a series of snapshots on a theme that only this photographer knows about. The awakening of ideas.</td>', 'Our eyes perceive this image in a pinwheel movement trying to find a resting place to give us an answer but there is not such thing and we are forever searching. There are all kinds of elements here. There is graciousness, power, tiredness, acceptance, fear, violence and in the end some hope. Its an imperfect photograph of an imperfect world. It belongs to a series of snapshots on a theme that only this photographer knows about. The awakening of ideas.', '2015-02-23 15:08:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(7320509, 1141879, 124815, '<td valign="top">Is this the Atwater vineyard? Am I missing the meaning of the title? At water? <br/> <br/>In any case, its solitary despair is beautiful and timeless. Its a place in a world, anywhere really, lost in time and engulfed in its seclusion. <br/> <br/>I got an even more intense feeling of suffocation when I cropped by mistake the bottom part of the picture.</td>', 'Is this the Atwater vineyard? Am I missing the meaning of the title? At water?  In any case, its solitary despair is beautiful and timeless. Its a place in a world, anywhere really, lost in time and engulfed in its seclusion.  I got an even more intense feeling of suffocation when I cropped by mistake the bottom part of the picture.', '2015-02-23 15:09:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(7320510, 1142090, 124815, '<td valign="top">I stopped at this image because in spite of its quite pedestrian title it contains something that I call sensory ghosts. <br/>A mundane scene fixed as if by mistake, incomplete and faulty but containing an uncanny feeling that makes one pause.</td>', 'I stopped at this image because in spite of its quite pedestrian title it contains something that I call sensory ghosts. A mundane scene fixed as if by mistake, incomplete and faulty but containing an uncanny feeling that makes one pause.', '2015-02-23 15:11:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(7320517, 1141931, 124815, '<td valign="top">An amusing street shot. Where would you find a man smoking pushing an old fashioned pram? In Liverpool or Manchester or even further North? Almost the Beatles era. Just wonderful.</td>', 'An amusing street shot. Where would you find a man smoking pushing an old fashioned pram? In Liverpool or Manchester or even further North? Almost the Beatles era. Just wonderful.', '2015-02-23 15:42:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(7320529, 1142090, 30364, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by mariuca:</b></div><hr/><i> ... in spite of its quite pedestrian title ... </i></td></tr></table> <br/>I so hope that that was an intentional pun.  It would be a wickedness worthy of Wilde if it were.</td>', 'Originally posted by mariuca: ... in spite of its quite pedestrian title ...  I so hope that that was an intentional pun.  It would be a wickedness worthy of Wilde if it were.', '2015-02-23 16:41:46.000000', NULL, 0),
